We may find it difficult to enroll patients in our clinical trials, which could delay or prevent clinical trials of our product candidates.
Identifying and qualifying patients to participate in clinical trials of our product candidates is critical to our success. The timing of our clinical trials
depends in part on the speed at which we can recruit patients to participate in testing our product candidates. If patients are unwilling to participate in our
clinical trials for a variety of reasons, including competitive clinical trials for similar patient populations, the timeline for recruiting patients, conducting
clinical trials and obtaining regulatory approval of potential products may be delayed. These delays could result in increased costs, delays in advancing our
product candidates, delays in testing the effectiveness of our technology or termination of the clinical trials altogether.
